  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "eeCLOUD 4.5.0 adds support for engine 0 (ServerType.eeCACHE) to connect to an eeCACHE service hosted on a server.\n- Configure Config.type = ServerType.eeCACHE, Config.server = \"host:7443\", and Config.username / Config.password with the service credentials. The default port is 7443; IPv6 uses \"[address]:port\".\n- Connections use authenticated gRPC over HTTP/2. Use \"https://host:7443\" for optional TLS with certificate validation.\n- The remote engine protocol maps all ISQLEngine operations. The eeCACHE service can use the existing eeCLOUD SQL engines internally; available behavior depends on the configured service mode and provider.\n- An empty Config.server preserves the injected local eeCACHE behavior. Remote connections never fall back to a direct client SQL connection.\nSee the package README, \"Remote engine\", for connection instructions. The eeCACHE service is separate from the NuGet package; see the official eeCLOUD website at https://eecloud.io.",
